Below is a **detailed and comprehensive Agile backlog** for your AI-powered construction marketplace app.
It includes **Epics → User Stories → Acceptance Criteria**, written in clear markdown so you can drop it directly into GitHub (e.g., `/docs/backlog.md`).

This backlog is designed for **MVP → V1 → V2** scalability and is formatted following best practices used by YC startups, Scrum teams, and product engineering groups.

---

# **NailiT Scope – Product Backlog (Epics & User Stories)**

*Last updated: 2025*

---

# **EPIC 1 — User Accounts & Authentication**

### **Goal:**

Enable homeowners and contractors to create accounts, log in, and manage their profile details securely.

---

## **User Story 1.1 — User Registration**

**As a** new user
**I want** to create an account with email/password
**So that** I can access the app.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* User can register with email, first name, last name, password.
* Validation for strong password.
* Unique email enforced.
* Email verification optional for MVP, required in V1.

---

## **User Story 1.2 — Login & Logout**

**As a** user
**I want** to log in and out securely
**So that** my session is protected.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Login API accepts email + password.
* Session token or JWT issued.
* Logout clears session/token.

---

## **User Story 1.3 — Profile Management**

**As a** user
**I want** to update my profile details
**So that** my information is accurate.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Edit name, phone, location, avatar.
* Delete account (soft delete).

---

# **EPIC 2 — Contractor Profiles & Skills**

### **Goal:**

Allow contractors to create professional profiles, upload photos/videos, list skills, and build trust.

---

## **User Story 2.1 — Create Contractor Profile**

**As a** contractor
**I want** to create a professional profile
**So that** homeowners can evaluate my skills.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Add company name, bio, experience, service area.
* Add license & insurance details.
* Data stored in `contractor_profiles`.

---

## **User Story 2.2 — Upload Contractor Portfolio Media**

**As a** contractor
**I want** to upload photos/videos of my work
**So that** I can showcase past projects.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Accepts multiple images/videos.
* Connects to cloud storage (S3).
* Displays media in portfolio gallery.

---

## **User Story 2.3 — Add Skills**

**As a** contractor
**I want** to tag my skills (e.g., drywall, plumbing)
**So that** I can be matched to the right projects.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Contractors can choose from predefined skills.
* Many-to-many relationship saved in `contractor_skills`.

---

## **User Story 2.4 — Contractor Minimum Job Size**

**As a** contractor
**I want** to set a minimum job value
**So that** I don't get small/unqualified leads.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Contractors can enter min job size in USD.
* Shown to homeowners when viewing contractor.

---

# **EPIC 3 — Project Creation & Photo Upload**

### **Goal:**

Enable homeowners to submit project details, upload photos, and prepare for analysis.

---

## **User Story 3.1 — Create a New Project**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to describe my project
**So that** I can receive AI analysis and contractor bids.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Form captures desc, budget, location, property type.
* Photos optional but accepted.
* Stored in `projects` & `project_media`.

---

## **User Story 3.2 — Upload Project Photos/Videos**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to upload photos
**So that** AI and contractors can better understand my project.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Upload multiple files.
* Save URLs to `project_media`.
* Preview before submitting.

---

# **EPIC 4 — AI Project Analyzer**

### **Goal:**

Provide homeowners with instant AI-generated scope, pricing, skillsets, questions, and a budget realism score.

---

## **User Story 4.1 — AI Scope of Work Generation**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** an AI-generated list of scope items
**So that** I understand what the project requires.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* AI returns structured bullet list of work tasks.
* Saved in `ai_analyses.scope_of_work_json`.

---

## **User Story 4.2 — AI Price Estimate**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** an estimated price range
**So that** I can tell if my budget is realistic.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* AI outputs min and max pricing.
* Display in UI.
* Save in `ai_analyses`.

---

## **User Story 4.3 — Budget Likelihood Score**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** a rating (Very Unlikely → Highly Likely)
**So that** I understand if my budget will attract skilled contractors.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Algorithm/AI returns correct likelihood.
* Save to `projects` + `ai_analyses`.
* Visual UI bar indicator.

---

## **User Story 4.4 — Recommended Skillsets**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to see required contractor skills
**So that** I hire someone qualified.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Skills generated by AI.
* Cross-map to platform skills list.

---

## **User Story 4.5 — Questions to Ask Contractors**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** a list of questions to ask during quotes
**So that** I avoid hiring unskilled contractors.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* 5–12 questions generated.
* Displayed in UI.
* Stored in `ai_analyses.questions_to_ask_json`.

---

# **EPIC 5 — Marketplace & Matching**

### **Goal:**

Connect homeowners with relevant contractors and enable discovery.

---

## **User Story 5.1 — Contractor Search**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to search contractors by skill or location
**So that** I can find qualified professionals.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Filter by skillset, service area, rating, min job size.
* Search results paginated.

---

## **User Story 5.2 — Contractor Profile View**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to view detailed contractor profiles
**So that** I can decide who to invite or hire.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Show portfolio, bio, skills, experience, reviews.

---

## **User Story 5.3 — Invite Contractors to Bid**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to invite specific contractors
**So that** I receive targeted bids.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Create `job_invites` entries.
* Contractors receive notifications.

---

# **EPIC 6 — Bidding System**

### **Goal:**

Enable contractors to bid on projects, and homeowners to compare and accept bids.

---

## **User Story 6.1 — Submit a Bid**

**As a** contractor
**I want** to submit a bid with notes and price
**So that** I can offer my services.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Create `bids` entry with amount, summary.
* Cannot submit >1 active bid per project.

---

## **User Story 6.2 — View All Bids**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to view all contractor bids
**So that** I can compare offers.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Display list with price, notes, contractor info.

---

## **User Story 6.3 — Accept a Bid**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to select the winning bid
**So that** the project can be awarded.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Creates `project_assignments`.
* Updates bid status to `accepted`.
* Notifies contractor.

---

## **User Story 6.4 — Decline Bids**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to decline bids I don’t accept
**So that** contractors know the status.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Updates bid status to `declined`.
* Sends a notification.

---

# **EPIC 7 — Messaging System**

### **Goal:**

Enable homeowners and contractors to communicate safely through the platform.

---

## **User Story 7.1 — Send Message**

**As a** user
**I want** to send messages to another user about a project
**So that** we can communicate without direct contact info.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Stored in `messages`.
* Must reference `project_id`.

---

## **User Story 7.2 — View Conversation**

**As a** user
**I want** to see all messages for a project
**So that** I can follow discussions.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Sort by timestamp.
* Mark messages as read when opened.

---

# **EPIC 8 — Reviews & Ratings**

### **Goal:**

Allow homeowners to review contractors after job completion.

---

## **User Story 8.1 — Leave a Review**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to rate the contractor
**So that** other users can evaluate them.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* 1–5 star rating + text comment.
* One review per project.
* Updates contractor’s average rating.

---

## **User Story 8.2 — View Contractor Reviews**

**As a** homeowner
**I want** to see reviews
**So that** I can assess quality.

**Acceptance Criteria**

* Reviews appear on contractor profile.

---

# **EPIC 9 — Notifications**

### **Goal:**

Keep users updated about invites, bids, messages, and assignment events.

---

## **User Story 9.1 — Receive Bid Notification**

Contractor → bid accepted
Homeowner → new bid received

---

## **User Story 9.2 — Receive Message Notification**

User notified when they receive a message.

---

## **User Story 9.3 — Job Invite Notification**

Contractor notified when homeowner invites them to bid.

---

# **EPIC 10 — Admin Management (Moderation)**

### **Goal:**

Maintain platform quality and compliance.

---

## **User Story 10.1 — Admin Login**

Admins can access moderation dashboard.

---

## **User Story 10.2 — Moderate Contractor Profiles**

Admins can:

* Approve/deny suspicious contractors
* Review license/insurance info

---

## **User Story 10.3 — Manage Project Reports**

Users can report:

* Fraud
* Low quality work
* Inappropriate content

Admins can investigate & resolve.

---

# **EPIC 11 — Payments & Escrow (Future V2)**

### **Goal:**

Enable deposits, escrow, milestone payments.

---

## **User Story 11.1 — Collect Deposit**

Homeowners can pay deposit through Stripe.

---

## **User Story 11.2 — Release Payments**

Milestone or final payment releases to contractor.

---

# **EPIC 12 — Feature Enhancements (Future)**

### Ideas included:

* 3D AI visualization of projects
* Permit requirements checker
* AI video analysis
* Contractor CRM tools
* Background checks
* Dispute resolution center

